New deputies begin at the entry-level rank and advance through demonstrated performance, activity, and supervisor recommendation.

## Rank Progression

| Rank | Description |
| --- | --- |
| **Deputy Sheriff Trainee** | Newly hired, completing field training with an FTO |
| **Deputy Sheriff** | Full patrol deputy after FTO sign-off |
| **Corporal** | Senior deputy with training and shift-lead responsibilities |
| **Sergeant** | First-line supervisor |
| **Lieutenant and above** | Station and command staff |

## Detective

Detective is an investigative assignment rather than a step in the patrol ladder. Deputies assigned to Criminal Investigations retain their rank and return to patrol if the assignment ends.

